      "text": "The vector corresponding to $(3,1)$ is $\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ As the distance between $\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{u}$ is $t,$ we have $\\mathbf{u} + t \\mathbf{d} = \\begin{pmatrix} x - 3 \\\\ y - 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$  Then $\\mathbf{d} = \\frac{1}{t} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{3}{t} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$ Since the slope of $\\mathbf{u}$ is $|\\mathbf{u}|^2 / vb,$ where $v$ is half the height of the parallelogram, we have $|\\frac{u + d}{t}|^2 = |\\frac{u + d}{t}|^2 = |\\mathbf{u}|^2 / vb$ is the slope of $\\mathbf{u} + t \\mathbf{d}.$  On the other hand (because $\\mathbf{d} = t + \\frac{3}{t} \\mathbf{v}$), we have $|\\mathbf{d}|^2 = |\\frac{3}{t} \\mathbf{v}|^2 + 2 \\frac{3}{t} (\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}) + \\frac{3^2}{t^2} |\\mathbf{u}|^2 + |\\frac{3}{t} \\mathbf{v}|^2 \\Longrightarrow |\\mathbf{d}|^2 = \\frac{9}{t^2} |\\mathbf{v}|^2 + \\frac{6}{t} (\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}) / |\\mathbf{d}| + \\frac{9}{t^2} |\\mathbf{v}|^2.$  Hence $|\\mathbf{d}|^2 / 9 = |\\mathbf{v}|^2 / (\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{d}) \\Longrightarrow \\mathbf{d} = |\\mathbf{v}| \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{3}{t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{t} \\end{pmatrix},$ so\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} + \\frac{1}{t} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]",
